                "explanation": "solutions[4].composition[6].concentration -> solutions[4].solutions[5].composition[0].concentration: Move y-aminobutyric acid from a flattened mix contribution into its single stock. Source 1.5500 g/50ml = 31 g/L stock. 0.00227 L stock / 0.05 L mix explains the former 1.4074 g/L direct contribution. NNM carrier constituents, where present, are separate and not included in this solute-only rate. Exact excerpt: \"y-aminobutyric acid (Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.) 1.5500 g/50ml - -\"; locator=sol-0 / recipe-23; table headings=['Compound', 'Amount', 'Unit', 'Conc. [g/L]', 'Conc. [mM]']. Exact excerpt: \"Add 2.27 ml of each carbon source\"; locator=sol-0 preparation step 9. Exact excerpt: \"Fill to 50 ml with NNM.\"; locator=sol-0 preparation step 9. User-contributed MediaDive P5 page, accessed 2026-10-07; source_type=user_contributed_dataset_page; page_sha256=fe4448ec7332d8e7ec8313b49ffa8e03b0c26ca54522d83fa802a19bbb25f5c7; figure_sha256=e90144dbb695abd6ac4279e294fe7b6b8a1b3d28dce4a26346fd14d78aa28917. Numeric evidence is the page text, not OCR of the inspected diagram. No journal validation or growth claim is implied.",
